Package: wifi-hotspot
Version: @VERSION@
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), hostapd, dnsmasq-base | dnsmasq, iw, iproute2, nftables | iptables, qrencode, pkexec | policykit-1
Recommends: python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-4.0, gir1.2-adw-1
Suggests: firewalld, network-manager
Maintainer: Carlos Del Rosario <65183782+CarlosDelRosario7@users.noreply.github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/CarlosDelRosario7/wifi-hotspot
Description: modern Wi-Fi hotspot manager for Linux
 WiFi Hotspot turns a Linux computer into a Wi-Fi access point. It supports
 Ethernet uplinks, concurrent AP+STA operation on one radio, and two wireless
 cards.
 .
 It provides a command-line interface, a small privileged daemon protected by
 polkit and a Unix socket, and a GTK4/Libadwaita interface. SSID, password,
 security, band, channel, country, DHCP, DNS, firewall, client list, traffic
 counters, QR sharing and profiles are configurable.
